WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:11.990
<b>The greatest souls are capable of the greatest vices as well as of the greatest virtues.</b>

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:11.990
RenГ© Descartes, "Discourse on Method"

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.490
S... Stop it!

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.520
What, you think we'll let you
off the hook if you cry enough?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.410
You're such a little coward, Karuizawa.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.400
Always hiding behind some man...

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.290
Yeah, it really pisses me off!

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.560
What happened to all that
fire you had before?

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.250
Hey, you listening?!

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.630
Th-That hurts!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.130
Wow, that face!

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.720
Maybe we should clean her up a little!

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.420
Great idea!

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.720
Let's do it!

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.970
Stop!

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.980
C'mon, look this way!

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.980
C'mon, Ayanokoji!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.140
Not yet.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.600
What an ugly pig!

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.610
Hilarious!

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.610
Enough already!

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.360
Hey, you three! What are you doing?

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.990
What are we doing?

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.590
We were just talking, right?

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.090
Right?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.870
Yeah.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.590
It's none of your business. Just butt out.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.170
We're going to make you apologize to Rika.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.900
You okay?

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.170
Leave me alone.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.580
I was just worried about you!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.170
Shut up!

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.670
I didn't ask for your help!

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.930
What the hell is her problem?!

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.020
<i>Perhaps I'll try it.</i>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.020
<b>Classroom
of
the
Elite</b>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.020
<b>2nd Season</b>

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.770
<b>Special Test
Day 3 (Rest Day)</b>

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.030
<b>Venus Group's Test</b>

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.490
<i>So the Venus Group's test
has concluded, as well.</i>

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.730
<i>Which means someone made a VIP accusation.</i>

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.040
<i>Class C really is the favorite.</i>

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.040
<i>Ryuen is trying to figure out the
principle behind VIP selections.</i>

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.020
<i>Which means I should add to the
pieces under my control while I can.</i>

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.470
<b><b>Sending</b></b>

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.430
<b>Manabe Shiho</b>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.430
<b><b>Sent</b></b>

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.340
<i>Now, let's see what happens.</i>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.980
What the heck? There's no signal down here.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.610
Why would Hirata-kun call
me to a place like this?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.110
H-How did you...

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.310
Shall we begin?

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.840
The "Karuizawa begs for mercy" photoshoot!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.850
Don't miss any great shots, Yamashita!

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.730
Okay!

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:13.080
Leave me alone.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.890
I haven't done anything wrong.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.170
Then why's your voice shaking?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.020
She's scared!

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.610
Aw, those knocking knees! Hilarious!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.610
What's the matter, Karuizawa?

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.610
Gonna cry? Gonna cry?!

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.370
I w-would never...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.310
I get this vibe from you...

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.340
You've been bullied, haven't you?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.870
You've been bullied, haven't you?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.740
Called it!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.700
She totally was!

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.120
You must be a pro at begging for mercy.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.750
So get to it already!

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.620
Beg for mercy!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.540
What are you talking about?

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.110
Beg for mercy!

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.110
I'm not going to

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.690
Let me go!

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.150
I said, head on the floor!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.220
Wow, gross.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.260
You take a shot, Rika.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.550
I-I'd rather not...

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.260
We're doing this for you!

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.260
Not like that.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.000
Like this!

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:29.350
Do that!

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.120
This is fun!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.370
<i>As demonstrated by the Milgram experiment,</i>

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.120
<i>circumstances can enhance
a person's natural cruelty.</i>

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.600
Now that's what I like to see!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.640
<i>Well done, Manabe.</i>

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.700
<b>Manabe Shiho</b>

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.580
<i>All I did was set the scene, and yet...</i>

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.650
<b>Manabe Shiho</b>

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.650
Subject:      <b>Karuizawa</b>

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.650
<b>I want revenge on Karuizawa as well.
I'll help you.</b>

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.650
Please... forgive me...

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.980
You could've just begged from the start!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:34.160
<i>Getting her to rock bottom will save me time.</i>

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.960
H-How did you...

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:02.680
Once a bullied child,
always a bullied child, it seems.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.190
You were watching all that?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.950
Don't bother calling Hirata.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.590
I know he's not really your boyfriend.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.460
And I know that you've been bullied.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:18.980
I know it all.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.170
That means I can expose you any time I like.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.070
What?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:35.140
To save yourself from
ever being bullied again,

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:39.150
you chose to hide your past and become
a parasite that attaches to others.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.100
But in the end...

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.100
Wh-What do you want? My body?

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:47.480
Now that you ask, I just might.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.570
Spread your legs.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.840
I don't accept this.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.420
You're not bullying me.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:21.350
You're just blackmailing me
into doing ridiculous things.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.850
You're not resisting, then?

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.750
Do you know what people do

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:32.740
when confronted by a reality
they can't do anything about?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.890
They stop resisting.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:39.240
"Ah, I'm being abused."

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.620
That thought fills their mind,
sterile and automatic.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.570
They don't scream, cry, or fight back.

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.250
They just accept it.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.260
What's the thing that's really hurting you?

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.720
Such fear, to the point of even
surrendering your body, is abnormal.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.330
I think there's something
bigger you're hiding.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.140
S-Stop...

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.110
Is this it? Is this your darkness?

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:13.100
Karuizawa... There exist
many kinds of despair.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:18.370
And what you've experienced
qualifies, without question.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.990
Those with darkness in their hearts
are naturally drawn together.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:27.290
And the stronger of the two
will always engulf the weaker.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:32.050
Wh-What are you... talking about?

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:36.420
The world contains darkness
greater than what you know.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.540
There's one thing I can promise you.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.140
Karuizawa.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.690
I will protect you from now on.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:55.010
In a far more reliable way than
Hirata or Machida could offer.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.420
<i>She totally was!</i>

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.950
<i>You must be a pro at begging for mercy.</i>

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.700
<i>So get to it already!</i>

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.800
The next time they come
after you, threaten them.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.540
<i>Beg for mercy!</i>

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.910
Tell them you'll release this footage.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.910
<i>Beg for mercy!</i>

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.040
Align yourself with me.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.860
There's something I need your help with.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.380
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.550
Class D can't ascend in its current form.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:24.360
But with you in control of the girls,

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:26.570
we can acquire the unity we've been lacking.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:30.560
<i>Yes. It's a role that Horikita can't perform.</i>

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.400
What in the world are you...

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:37.710
I'll act in your interest,
and you'll act in mine.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.130
That's the relationship
you were after, isn't it?

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:46.850
All right...

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.040
But what do you want me to do?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.290
To begin with, I'd like to win this test.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.070
After all, you are...

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.100
Sorry for the wait.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:09.520
How can I help you?

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.460
There's something I'd
like to buy with points.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:18.030
<b>2nd Season</b>

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:18.030
<b>Classroom
of
the
Elite</b>

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.280
<b>Special Test
Day Four</b>

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.280
<b>Minutes Before
Final Discussion</b>

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:25.530
Beaten here, eh?

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.500
Oh, good morning!

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.680
Hey, sorry to hog the couch.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.690
It's fine, really.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.320
Would you like to talk a
bit before the discussion?

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:12.020
There's something I've
been dying to ask you.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:12.830
Ask me?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:13.710
Yeah.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:17.350
You really want to reach Class A, right?

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.780
I suppose.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.460
I'll bet you do!

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.190
I do, too.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:25.090
I have a dream to graduate
as part of Class A.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.220
But since we're in different classes,

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.910
I guess only one of us can
make our dream come true, huh?

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.210
I suppose.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.860
Though there is one exceptional means...

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:41.860
Saving up 20 million
private points, right?

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.000
Yes, although apparently,
no one's ever done it before.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:47.240
It's such a tremendous amount.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.740
Ayanokoji-kun.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:53.450
You did see my points that time, didn't you?

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:56.890
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to pry.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.310
<i>That's right.</i>

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.750
<b>Exchanging Points</b>

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.750
<b>Ichinose Honami</b>

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:01.250
<i>At the time of the end of the first term,</i>

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:03.960
<i>Ichinose had a tremendous number of points.</i>

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.070
I'm not accusing you.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:11.030
But I can't tell you any more than that.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.420
And I won't pry.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.890
Hey, Ayanokoji. You're already here?

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.400
All alone with Ichinose-dono?!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:25.290
Have we intruded upon a secret tryst?!

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:26.910
Oh, no...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.910
Of course not!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.660
<b>Special Test
Final Discussion Begins</b>

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.660
It's time to get started.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.430
I think Hamaguchi-kun has a proposal to make.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:46.480
We're aiming for a victory in which we all
unite to correctly guess the VIP, right?

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.130
Where's this coming from?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.680
Indeed, this is the very
motive for our discussions!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.910
We're not going to reach a conclusion
in the remaining time that way.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:59.490
So I think we're going to have to buckle
down and try a different method.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:01.310
A different method?

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:04.070
I think you know exactly what I mean.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.070
We'll show each other our cell phones.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.850
It's impossible to falsify the
email from the school telling us

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.960
if we're the VIP or not.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.830
We can see at a glance who the VIP is.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.720
Ridiculous.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:21.210
Then whoever outs the VIP first will
get all the points to themselves.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.740
If there's even one traitor, it's over.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:26.010
I'm well aware of that.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.220
But playing it safe won't
get us anywhere, either.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.510
You're talking about making a gamble?

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.360
Yes.

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:34.410
Obviously, the VIP themselves and those

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.770
trying to protect them will be
reticent to show their phones.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.390
What shall we do?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.900
That should let us narrow it down, at least.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.400
You think we're all going to
go in on such a high-risk plan?

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.100
You seem awfully upset about it, Machida-kun.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:46.990
What?

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:51.660
If it ends in a deadlock with
nobody getting class points,

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.870
that's a net positive for Class A.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:15:01.040
Conversely, the rest of us have
a reason to want to take a risk.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.140
She has a point.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.140
<i>Ichinose is behind this.</i>

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:07.550
<i>She's using Hamaguchi to
get her plan out there.</i>

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:11.070
No one has to show their
phone who doesn't want to.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.010
But since it was my idea, I'll show mine.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.800
From: Advanced Nurturing High School
Regarding the Special Test

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.300
Hamaguchi-kun!

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.810
I'll show mine, too!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.310
I'm not the VIP.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.050
Can this be true?!

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:24.140
<i>Everyone in Class B is showing theirs.</i>

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.820
<i>Which means...</i>

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.060
Very well.

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:29.070
I'll participate, as well.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.450
Ayanokoji?!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.110
Ayanokoji-kun? You're sure?

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:33.900
Yes.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:37.950
So you're not the VIP, either...

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.660
I'll participate, as well.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.200
Are you nuts?

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.920
If we let it end like this,
the VIP is the only one that benefits.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.430
Or are <i>you</i> the VIP?

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:50.970
O-Of course not!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.630
I'll show mine, too.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.640
I want points.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.410
Fine! I'll show you!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.270
A wise man once said,
"If you can't beat them, join them!"

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.340
It's not me, either!

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:09.400
Which means that,
other than Class A, it's down to...

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.900
Hang on. Don't tell me...

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.230
Promise me, everyone.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.160
Promise me you won't out the VIP early.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.470
Yukimura, you're...

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:26.680
I'm sorry I lied to you, Ayanokoji.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.300
Regarding the Special Test
Attention, students.

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:29.880
I'm the VIP.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.730
I-Incredible!

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.050
I can't believe it.

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:40.420
<i>An excellent performance.</i>

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.370
<i>Our victory is now assured.</i>

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.390
Guys, let's all agree not
to expose Yukimura-kun.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.240
Let's complete the test together!

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.610
Well... maybe...

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.930
Thank you, everyone.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.030
I want to have faith.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:58.790
No, I <i>choose</i> to have faith!

00:16:59.240 --> 00:16:59.820
Sure.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:00.910
You said it!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.660
We shan't betray your trust!

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.810
<i>It's not going to happen.</i>

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.630
<i>Someone's going to betray
the others to get the points.</i>

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.670
<i>And then... they'll fall for the trap.</i>

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.920
<i>Yukimura isn't the VIP.</i>

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.930
<i>I told him I was the VIP,</i>

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.590
<i>and got him to trade cell phones.</i>

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.210
<i>I didn't anticipate Ichinose's
actions, but this way...</i>

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.440
Ichinose Honami

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:35.200
That's actually Ayanokoji-kun's
cell phone, isn't it?

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.950
W-Well, I...

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.840
The number I just called
is Ayanokoji-kun's number.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.700
Because I don't know
Yukimura-kun's number yet!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.600
<b>Ayanokoji-kun</b>

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.960
Which means Ayanokoji-kun is the real VIP!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.670
Ayanokoji-dono is...

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.090
...the VIP?

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:55.340
So that's it.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.530
You mean you were lying before?!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:59.330
Explain yourselves, Class D!

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:02.220
I-I swear, I knew nothing...

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.690
<i>The discussion period is now over.</i>

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:07.900
<i>The groups will disperse
and return to their rooms.</i>

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.280
Damn it!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:11.480
What a bunch of filthy cheaters Class D are.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:09.580
<i>I repeat.</i>

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:13.630
<i>The groups will disperse
and return to their rooms.</i>

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.730
I guess we see what your
"faith in us" is worth.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:21.370
Well, let's hope nobody breaks your trust.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.390
This is the worst possible case!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.480
Guess it all went well, huh?

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.010
Yes.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.820
Exactly what we wanted.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:49.770
After all... you are the VIP, Karuizawa.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.020
How did you know that?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.930
Hirata told me.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.630
Let's use that fact to set
a double-layered trap.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:01.780
First, you and I will trade cell phones.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:02.490
VIP

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.060
I'll pretend to be the VIP,

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.630
and trade cell phones
once again with Yukimura.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.790
I won't tell Yukimura about you, either.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.650
Then we'll steer the discussion

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:15.040
in a way that gets Yukimura
to volunteer himself as VIP.

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:18.240
So if someone exposes Yukimura-kun,

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.910
or sees through his trade with you,

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:22.720
they'll fall into the trap?

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:25.310
But there's a hole in this plan.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:29.030
Even if we trade phones,
we can't change our phone numbers.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.310
If someone calls one of us, we're outed.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.060
What do we do, then?

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.570
We'll exchange SIM cards.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:40.320
But aren't the SIM cards in the
school-provided cell phones locked?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.590
There's nothing that points can't buy you.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.980
That's the fundamental rule of this school.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:49.900
I expect I can buy the unlock
method from Ms. Chabashira.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.460
I feel a little bad for Yukimura-kun, though.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.460
Yeah, same!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.040
Ichinose-san?!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:03.870
After a lie is exposed, people will
perceive any subsequent answer as truth.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.350
Someone's definitely falling right
into your trap about now!

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:10.850
Is that why you called my phone?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.600
Was Class B going to try the very same plan?

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.780
Got me, huh?

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:21.310
But if you knew our plan,
why didn't you point it out?

00:20:21.310 --> 00:20:22.910
Isn't it obvious?

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:26.620
Whether the false accusation
comes from Class A or Class C,

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.520
it's still a net benefit to my class.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:34.620
And the reason you let the discussion
stall was to pull this from the end?

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.790
Something like that.

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:40.760
Hey, did Horikita-san come
up with this plan, too?

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.130
Who else would?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.370
I see, I see...

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.140
Hey, is this...

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.770
From: Advanced Nurturing High School
Subject: Regarding the Special Test

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.770
What happened?

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.980
Class C won?

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.490
And Class A totally whiffed it!

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:06.010
It's what we were after. But...

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.660
I like that look on your face...

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.580
Suzune.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:17.380
As you can see,
I knew exactly who the VIP was.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:24.270
But we didn't have a traitor in our group.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.880
If you'd known who it was,
you would have betrayed us.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.310
Kushida Kikyo.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:29.810
Wasn't it?

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.050
I realized on the second day

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:36.270
that Kushida was the VIP.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.440
How?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.380
It was all too obvious.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.650
You're awfully transparent.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:46.150
That expression of yours is so sexy.

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:50.300
You'll be my next target.

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:54.610
I'll tear you apart, body and soul.

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.750
Look forward to the second
term with great anticipation.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:07.050
<i>Class D might be in a
difficult position soon.</i>
